    "body": "Commit 1 of 3 for ADR-029. **Parser-side only, behavior-neutral** — the layout engine is unchanged. Flex elements still fall through to block layout until Commit 2 adds the algorithm and dispatch.\n\n## Summary\n\n- `Display::Flex` + `Display::InlineFlex` added to the enum\n- `display_of` recognizes `flex` → `Display::Flex` and `inline-flex` → `Display::InlineFlex`\n- `flex` shorthand expansion: `flex: A` / `A B` / `A B C` / `auto` / `none` / `initial` → 3 longhands\n- `flex-flow` shorthand expansion: `<dir>` / `<wrap>` / `<dir> <wrap>` (either order) → 2 longhands\n- 14 new stylesheet tests\n\n## Design\n\nBoth shorthands expand via `try_expand_flex` / `try_expand_flex_flow` helpers next to the existing `try_expand_grid_template`, following the ADR-012/ADR-028 convention of shorthand-to-longhand expansion at parse time. Malformed forms drop the declaration entirely (same as `grid-template` in ADR-028).\n\n## The one test touch\n\n`test_layout.cpp`'s `display_of: unknown value falls back to Block` test had input `display: flex` — genuinely unknown at the time ADR-028 wrote the ADR-028 note. Flex is now supported, so the input moves to `display: inline-block` (still genuinely unknown, not planned for v1). The test's contract is preserved; the comment now records both the ADR-028 and ADR-029 transitions.\n\n**This is the self-correcting pattern this arc has codified:** the historical record reflects the transition, and the test's contract is preserved, not weakened. Not a regression — the process working.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-029: 365 cases, 1508 assertions\n- After Commit 1: **379 cases, 1575 assertions**\n- All pass, zero warnings\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| This PR | Parser-side: enum + display_of + shorthand expansion + 14 tests |\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `display: flex` → `Display::Flex` | ✅ |\n| `display: inline-flex` → `Display::InlineFlex` | ✅ |\n| `flex: 1 1 100%` (Wikipedia's actual form) expands to 3 longhands | ✅ |\n| `flex-flow: row nowrap` expands to 2 longhands | ✅ |\n| `flex: auto` / `none` / `initial` keywords | ✅ |\n| Malformed forms drop declaration | ✅ |\n| **No layout behavior change** | ✅ (verified by full suite) |\n| No switch-on-Display breakage | ✅ (grep confirms none exists) |\n\n## What's next (Commit 2)\n\n`layout_flex_children` — the algorithm. Row/column direction, `justify-content` (5 values + `end` alias), `align-items` (3 values + stretch default), `flex-grow`/`flex-shrink`/`flex-basis`, gaps. Dispatch from `layout_element` on `Display::Flex` / `Display::InlineFlex`. This is where the Wikipedia header collapses from 585px → ~50-100px and article content moves above the fold.\n\nRefs #161",
